---
description: Best practices for React component development
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}
---
- **Functional Components with Hooks:** Use functional components with hooks instead of class components
- **Single Responsibility Components:** Keep components small and focused on a single responsibility
- **Performance Optimization:** Utilize memoization with `useMemo`, `useCallback`, and `memo` for performance
- **State Management Strategy:** Use React Context for simple state, Zustand for complex global state
- **React 19 Features Adoption:** Leverage new React 19 features like improved SSR and automatic batching
- **Document & Error Boundaries:** Implement error boundaries for graceful error handling in component trees
- **Client/Server Component Separation:** Clearly mark 'use client' directives only where needed
- **React Hooks Rules:** Follow React hooks rules (call only at top level, only in React functions)
- **Custom Hook Development:** Extract reusable logic into custom hooks with descriptive names
- **Conditional Rendering Practices:** Use clean patterns for conditional rendering like ternaries or logical AND
- **Controlled Form Components:** Prefer controlled components for form inputs with validation patterns
- **React DevTools Usage:** Use React DevTools for debugging and performance profiling
- **Component Props Documentation:** Document component props with TypeScript interfaces and JSDoc comments
- **Component Testing Strategy:** Test components focusing on user interactions rather than implementation details